+// browser#103 (0077-B, the E0 fold-in). Answer once the answer is knowable,
+// instead of answering fast and wrong.
+//
+// Observed while running E0 on a cold profile: the first page load probed this
+// roughly four seconds BEFORE xrWeaveBindWindowDXR completed, was told no,
+// activated nothing, and never asked again — a reload wove instantly. That is
+// the same family of bug as #103 itself (support state answered before it is
+// knowable), and it has to be fixed HERE rather than by re-announcing later:
+// nothing in the renderer-facing surface can push a correction to a page that
+// has already been told no, and building one would mean changing blink mojom.
+//
+// The client runs the callback on this sequence — immediately when it already
+// knows (a session has come up, or init finished without one), otherwise when
+// the session binds or after a short bounded deadline, whichever is first. It is
+// never dropped, so the renderer's promise always settles.
 void DisplayXRServiceImpl::IsInline3DSupported(
     IsInline3DSupportedCallback callback) {
-  std::move(callback).Run(DisplayXRWeaveClient::IsSupported());
+  DisplayXRWeaveClient::RequestSupportWhenKnown(std::move(callback));
 }
 
